From 59197c158388f6113714f15652548b3a56480c9e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex Experiment <codex-experiment@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:41:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt6797: indicate PM connection from a fresh owned
 beacon before keys

The current initial-GTK join sends BSS and station records but omits the
public gen3 PM connection indication. Latch a unique valid TIM DTIM from
an existing qualified post-association target beacon. The association
callback waits within its existing station phase deadline, then sends
0x16 through the current sequence/page-credit owner before returning to
key installation. Zero ATIM/UAPSD fit the admitted legacy no-PS profile.

Require the credited indication at key admission. A metadata/submission/
credit failure stops before keys. Add the corresponding credited PM abort
under the existing quiescent healthy-cleanup ledger before key/STA/BSS
removal. The six cleanup commands fit the unchanged 2500 ms grant tail;
all phase, transaction, frame, lifetime and resource limits stay unchanged.
No event family, key reuse or reconnect is enabled by this change.

Internal experiment archive, synthetic non-certifying author identity;
no DCO certification and not an upstream submission.
